"Let $S_n$ be the symmetric group, let $\\Phi_w$ denote the principal specialization of the Schubert polynomial at $q=-1$, and let $\\mathcal{DL}_n$ denote the set of doubly layered permutations. Define\n\n$$\n\\widetilde{u}(n):=\\max_{w\\in S_n}\\Phi_w,\\qquad \\widetilde{v}(n):=\\max_{w\\in\\mathcal{DL}_n}\\Phi_w.\n$$\n\n**Doubly layered maximizer conjecture.** For every $n$, all permutations reaching the maximum $\\widetilde{u}(n)$ are doubly layered permutations. Thus, there is a limit\n\n$$\n\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\frac{\\log_2\\widetilde{u}(n)}{n^2}.\n$$\n\nThe paper proves the corresponding asymptotic formula for the doubly layered maximum $\\widetilde{v}(n)$, but the unrestricted maximization and the asserted limit remain open."